From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pi-hrx-fabric <fabric@1bit.local>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:47:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] accel/amdxdna: two TDR-recovery outcomes are not failures

0007's recovery latches hw_dead ("the NPU array is unusable until the driver is
reloaded", every later create_context/submit refused -ENODEV) for two cases that
are not recovery failures:

1. A power-cycle inside the 60 s rate-limit window. aie2_hw_reset() answers
   -EBUSY, and aie2_tdr_recover_all() counted that as "recovery failed". With
   tdr_timeout_ms=15000 the watchdog ticks four times inside the window, so any
   two TDRs within 60 s killed the array (measured 2026-11-04 22:28 on
   strixhalo). Throttled means "retry on the next watchdog tick": check it
   before tearing any context down, touch nothing, and leave the pending jobs
   pending - the array has not been power-cycled yet, so restarting contexts
   against it is the one thing that must not happen.

2. A context whose client is already closing: its heap has no host buffer
   address left (the client's VMAs are gone), so aie2_hwctx_restart() refuses it
   -ENODEV before talking to the firmware. That is a context being torn down,
   not a failed recovery: skip it (its jobs were already unpaused by the restart
   call, so a waiter fails rather than hangs) and keep the recovered array
   usable. Measured 2026-11-04 21:50:23 (one context) and 22:40 (two) - ordinary
   multi-client use - each time after a power-cycle that had SUCCEEDED.

Both are the difference between "one request died" and "the NPU is gone for
every lane until a reload". hw_dead is cleared only by aie2_start()
(aie2_pci.c), i.e. by a device resume or a module reload, so leaving it latched
costs every client on the box until then.

The throttle predicate is factored out (aie2_hw_reset_throttled) so aie2_hw_reset()
and the TDR path cannot disagree about what a -EBUSY means.

Signed-off-by: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.c | 18 +++++++++++--
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.h |  1 +
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.c b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.c
index 666f5a54..ac4919e7 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.c
@@ -517,6 +517,21 @@ static int aie2_hw_resume(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna)
  * Return: 0 if the firmware was reloaded (or there was nothing to reset),
  * -EBUSY if the rate limit skipped it, or the error from the reload.
  */
+/*
+ * aie2_hw_reset_throttled - is a power-cycle still inside the rate-limit window?
+ *
+ * The rate limit is a safety valve, not a recovery failure: a caller that is told
+ * "throttled" knows the array was power-cycled less than
+ * AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS ago and must retry later rather than conclude
+ * that recovery is impossible. aie2_hw_reset() and the TDR path ask this one
+ * predicate so the two can never disagree about which case a -EBUSY is.
+ */
+bool aie2_hw_reset_throttled(struct amdxdna_dev_hdl *ndev)
+{
+	return time_before(jiffies,
+			   ndev->last_reset_jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS));
+}
+
 int aie2_hw_reset(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna)
 {
 	struct amdxdna_dev_hdl *ndev = xdna->dev_handle;
@@ -527,8 +542,7 @@ int aie2_hw_reset(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna)
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	if (time_before(jiffies, ndev->last_reset_jiffies +
-				msecs_to_jiffies(AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS))) {
+	if (aie2_hw_reset_throttled(ndev)) {
 		XDNA_WARN(xdna, "NPU reset skipped: last reset %d ms ago",
 			  jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - ndev->last_reset_jiffies));
 		return -EBUSY;
diff --git a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.h b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.h
index c5977f3b..13641108 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.h
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_pci.h
@@ -321,6 +321,7 @@ void aie2_hwctx_suspend(struct amdxdna_client *client);
 int aie2_hwctx_resume(struct amdxdna_client *client);
 int aie2_hwctx_restart(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna, struct amdxdna_hwctx *hwctx);
 #define AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS	60000
+bool aie2_hw_reset_throttled(struct amdxdna_dev_hdl *ndev);
 int aie2_hw_reset(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna);
 int aie2_cmd_submit(struct amdxdna_hwctx *hwctx, struct amdxdna_sched_job *job, u64 *seq);
 int aie2_hwctx_heap_expand(struct amdxdna_hwctx *hwctx, struct amdxdna_gem_obj *heap);
diff --git a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
index 4cc3d461..8d0878e8 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
@@ -122,11 +122,33 @@ struct aie2_tdr_resume_arg {
 static int aie2_tdr_resume_hwctx(struct amdxdna_hwctx *hwctx, void *arg)
 {
 	struct aie2_tdr_resume_arg *rarg = arg;
+	struct amdxdna_dev *xdna = rarg->xdna;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = aie2_hwctx_restart(rarg->xdna, hwctx);
+	ret = aie2_hwctx_restart(xdna, hwctx);
 	if (ret) {
-		XDNA_ERR(rarg->xdna, "%s restart failed, ret %d", hwctx->name, ret);
+		/*
+		 * A context whose client is already tearing down has no host buffer
+		 * address left to map (the client's VMAs are gone), so it cannot be
+		 * restarted - and does not need to be: the process it belongs to is
+		 * gone, and aie2_hwctx_restart() unpaused its jobs before returning,
+		 * so anything still waiting on it fails instead of hanging.
+		 *
+		 * Counting this as a recovery failure is what turned one dying
+		 * context into "the NPU array is unusable until the driver is
+		 * reloaded" for every other client on the box: measured 2026-11-04
+		 * 21:50:23 and again at 22:40 on strixhalo, a TDR recovery whose
+		 * power-cycle SUCCEEDED (ret 0) was reported as failed because of
+		 * one or two closing contexts, and every later open was refused
+		 * -ENODEV until a module reload.
+		 */
+		if (amdxdna_obj_dma_addr(hwctx->priv->heap) == AMDXDNA_INVALID_ADDR) {
+			XDNA_WARN(xdna,
+				  "%s has no host buffer address (client closing): not restarting it, the recovered array stays usable",
+				  hwctx->name);
+			return 0;
+		}
+		XDNA_ERR(xdna, "%s restart failed, ret %d", hwctx->name, ret);
 		rarg->failed = true;
 	}
 
@@ -142,6 +164,25 @@ static void aie2_tdr_recover_all(struct amdxdna_dev *xdna)
 	bool fw_dead = false;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A power-cycle inside the rate-limit window is throttled, not failed
+	 * (aie2_hw_reset() would return -EBUSY). Check it before tearing anything
+	 * down: stopping the contexts and then discovering the array was not
+	 * power-cycled leaves every client holding a destroyed context, and
+	 * counting the -EBUSY as "recovery failed" latched hw_dead for the whole
+	 * array - two TDRs inside the 60 s window were enough, which is exactly
+	 * what happens with tdr_timeout_ms=15000 (measured 2026-11-04 22:28 on
+	 * strixhalo). Nothing is touched here; the next watchdog tick retries and
+	 * the pending jobs stay pending until then.
+	 */
+	if (aie2_hw_reset_throttled(ndev)) {
+		XDNA_WARN(xdna,
+			  "TDR recovery throttled: last power-cycle %u ms ago (< %d ms), retrying on the next watchdog tick",
+			  jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - ndev->last_reset_jiffies),
+			  AIE2_HW_RESET_MIN_INTERVAL_MS);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	amdxdna_for_each_client(xdna, client)
 		amdxdna_hwctx_walk(client, &fw_dead, NULL, aie2_tdr_stop_hwctx);
 
-- 
2.53.0

